.Dd July 22, 2026
.Dt OCIFBSD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ocifbsd
.Nd FreeBSD native OCI runtime
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl vhV
.Ar command
.Op Ar arguments
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a FreeBSD-native OCI (Open Container Initiative) runtime.
It maps OCI bundles to
.Xr jail 8
parameters, manages container lifecycle state under
.Pa /var/run/ocifbsd ,
and applies host-side mounts (nullfs, devfs, procfs, tmpfs, fdescfs)
into the container rootfs on start.
.Pp
The following commands are available:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Cm create Oo Fl n Ar name Oc Ar bundle
Create a container from an OCI bundle.
The jail is created with
.Cm persist
so it remains until
.Cm start
or
.Cm delete .
Prints the 64-hex container id on stdout.
.It Cm start Ar container-id
Start a created container (attach init process, apply mounts).
.It Cm kill Ar container-id Op Fl s Ar signal
Send a signal to the container init process.
Default is SIGTERM.
Idempotent for already-stopped or never-started containers.
.It Cm delete Ar container-id Op Fl f
Delete a container and unmount applied mounts.
Use
.Fl f
to force deletion of a running container.
.It Cm state Ar container-id
Show the current state of a container.
.It Cm list
List known containers from the state directory.
.It Cm inspect Ar container-id
Show detailed container metadata as JSON.
.It Cm run Oo Fl n Ar name Oc Ar bundle
Create and start a container in one command.
.It Cm pull Oo Fl n | -dry-run Oc Ar reference
Parse an OCI image reference and print registry, repository, tag, and
store path (default
.Pa /var/lib/ocifbsd ,
overridable with
.Ev OCIFBSD_DATA_DIR ) .
With
.Fl n
only resolve and print.
Without
.Fl n ,
fetch the manifest and layers via the OCI Distribution API into that path.
.It Cm load Oo Fl n Ar reference Oc Ar archive
Import a local OCI image into the image store.
.Ar archive
may be a directory in OCI image-layout form
.Pq Pa oci-layout , index.json , blobs/
or a
.Pa .tar , .tar.gz ,
or
.Pa .tar.xz
archive of that layout, such as the container images published at
.Pa https://download.freebsd.org/releases/OCI-IMAGES/ .
The image layers are verified against their manifest digests and unpacked
into a rootfs, and a runtime
.Pa config.json
is generated from the image configuration, so the result can be run with
.Cm create Fl Fl image
or
.Cm run Fl Fl image .
With
.Fl n
the store entry is named by the given reference instead of the archive's
.Li org.opencontainers.image.ref.name
annotation.
.It Cm images
List top-level entries under the local image store
.Pq Pa /var/lib/ocifbsd .
An empty or missing store is not an error.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
Global options (before the command):
.Bl -tag -width ".Fl v"
.It Fl v , -verbose
Enable verbose output.
.It Fl h , -help
Show help message and exit.
.It Fl V , -version
Show version information and exit.
.El
.Pp
Subcommand options:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl n Ar name , -name Ar name
Human-readable name for
.Cm create
and
.Cm run
(also used in jail naming).
.It Fl s Ar signal , -signal Ar signal
Signal for
.Cm kill
(number or name).
.It Fl f , -force
Force
.Cm delete
of a running container.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Create a container from an OCI bundle:
.Bd -literal
ocifbsd create --name my-container /path/to/bundle
.Ed
.Pp
Start, inspect state, signal, and delete:
.Bd -literal
ocifbsd start <id>
ocifbsd state <id>
ocifbsd kill <id>
ocifbsd delete --force <id>
.Ed
.Pp
Create and run in one command:
.Bd -literal
ocifbsd run --name web /path/to/bundle
.Ed
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width ".Pa /var/run/ocifbsd" -compact
.It Pa /var/run/ocifbsd/
Runtime state directory (per-container JSON)
.It Pa /var/lib/ocifbsd/
Image and volume data directory (future image store)
.It Pa /etc/ocifbsd/
Configuration directory (reserved)
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr jail 8 ,
.Xr jail 3 ,
.Xr mount 8 ,
.Xr rctl 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
was developed to provide native OCI runtime support for FreeBSD.
Phase 1 acceptance covers create/start/state/kill/delete with ATF
unit and root integration tests on FreeBSD lab hosts.
.Sh AUTHORS
.Nm
was developed by Klara, Inc. under sponsorship from the FreeBSD Foundation,
with REVYTECH, Inc. lifecycle and test work on
.Li feature/oci-bootstrap .
